B7 — hubble external surface, exact output identity vs the v1.15 reference wires
  Input: the wire-decoded pixels (lossless round trip) of the reference
  maximum wire /tmp/r9f_new_maximum.mnf8 (1,452,400 B,
  sha256 27f7d2229cd32dd81464f292c0d73df5a3b2b8530b96398c18e2e63ed344efd1).
  maximum : re-encoded → 1,452,400 B, cmp == the reference wire BYTE-IDENTICAL
            (verify PASS: exact RGB8 reconstruction, 1000x872, 3465 tiles);
            585.9 s wall (554.6 s user), RSS 136.5 MB (idle machine).
  balanced: re-encoded → 1,502,259 B (66249fbe75a07b20dc484055e03cbbfba0b4518863afd962175aa3010efcb118),
            cmp == /tmp/r9f_new_balanced.mnf8 BYTE-IDENTICAL; 152.6 s, RSS 134.3 MB.
